{"term":"hull","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:3e569220e65246a88e","definition":"The outer covering of a fruit or seed.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["peel","husk","shell"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bean-hull","hully","soyhull","rice hull"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hull#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b3189a675c09e4eb91","definition":"Any covering.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bean-hull","hully","soyhull","rice hull"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hull#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3854cd393a4f0130df","definition":"To remove the outer covering of a fruit or seed.","example":"She sat on the back porch hulling peanuts.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["peel","husk","shell","shuck"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bean-hull","hully","soyhull","rice hull"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hull#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5874d85faf854554c3","definition":"The body or frame of a vessel, such as a ship or plane.","example":"VVhen you haue berthed or brought her [the ship] vp to the planks, vvhich are thoſe thicke timbers vvhich goeth fore and aft on each ſide, vvhereon doth lie the beames of the firſt Orlop, vvhich is the firſt floore to ſupport the plankes doth couer the Hovvle, thoſe are great croſſe timbers, that keepes the ſhip ſides aſunder, the maine beame is euer next the maine maſt, […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":["fuselage"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bean-hull","hully","soyhull","rice hu